      "math_academy_id": "e-14170",
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $f$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $-1$ | $4$ | $3$ | $-1$ | $4$ | $2$ | $0$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $f(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{ -1,0,2,3,4  \\}.$",
